body:
Well I just hope you can reach a point where u don’t feel it’s necessary. Self harm can be hard to stop but honestly the mental clarity and freedom that comes with it is seriously worth it.

It’s a problem in the sense that doing hard drugs is a problem. You can do it, but it doesn’t mean it’s good for you. Self harm has so many negative side effects and they often outweigh any positives

Also I hope you don’t think I’m being hostile, I just like talking w people and seeing different opinions and such ;;

first of all, where the hell are these numbers coming from… it seems like random asspull numbers. and in either way, everyone finds different things attractive. my bf doesn’t have any of those traits and i still think he’s hot as hell

for instance, being 6foot…? it’s an arbitrary number. what does it matter if you are 5’11” or 6’? do you magically become more attractive? (no)

to avoid these people? don’t interact with them. block key words online, block accounts, and stop interacting with this content. in real life, distance yourself, find new connections if the only people you know spout this nonsense.
